From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:50:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: skip the load and store of depth/stencil aspects a
 pass never touches

DXVK binds the game's depth-stencil view to every pass, also to passes
none of whose draws enable the depth or stencil test. Hades (D3D11, the
rpcount build, about 228 fps) has 32.5k passes/s, 18.9k of them with a
depth attachment: 16.6k/s LOAD + DONT_CARE, 2.25k/s CLEAR + STORE, and no
draw in any of them touches depth. 18.9k passes/s run a preload, and 2.26M
of the 3.1M tiles walked per second are preloaded: almost all of it a
late-ZS depth reload nobody reads.

A depth or stencil aspect that is loaded (LOAD_OP_LOAD, or the forced
preload of DONT_CARE/NONE with STORE_OP_NONE) or stored but that nothing in
the pass reads or writes now has its preload, its write-back and its
incremental-rendering spills dropped. With storeOp DONT_CARE the contents
are undefined anyway; with STORE or NONE they must equal the loaded ones,
which memory already holds: not writing them back leaves the plane and its
AFBC headers byte for byte as they were (Z/S planes have no CRC).

"Touched" is conservative, from the state each draw (API or vk_meta) is
recorded with: the depth test (depth writes need it) or depth bounds test
enabled, a fragment shader reading depth (input attachment, tile read),
rasterization-order depth access; stencil likewise with the stencil test.
vkCmdClearAttachments of the aspect and any vkCmdExecuteCommands in the
pass count as touching it. Candidates are fixed at vkCmdBeginRendering:
separate Z/S planes, no CLEAR load op, no resolve, no multisampled render
to single sampled, no multiview, no suspend/resume, not a secondary
continuing a pass, and only on v11/v12 (v10 bakes FBD words into its CRC
patch commands; v13+ HSR and v14 layer state aren't covered).

The FBDs are emitted at the first draw, before the pass's use is known.
get_fb_descs() now emits them with the candidates untouched so far dropped,
the final answer for most passes. If a later draw touches a dropped aspect,
vkCmdEndRendering restores its load/store and writes the main and IR FBD
sets again in place (new emit_fb_desc_sets(), split out of get_fb_descs()):
the command stream refers to them by address only and patches them (tiler
pointer of simultaneous-use copies, CRC init, provoking vertex) when it
runs, and their tag, size and layout follow the formats, not the Z/S
load/store. Nothing else recorded during the pass reads that state.

Compatibility channel. PANVK_NO_ZS_UNTOUCHED_SKIP=1 restores the old
behaviour.

